{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785102299,"nonce":"CUI3gVCcLFNn5D/EdyM+gtV05jI=","title":"ADR-0061 **s8** (content identity beside the snapshot root, closing `945b1f4`)","message":"is proven at two grains — the real CAS (`scarab-storage-s3/tests/hashing.rs`)\nand the real engine over real Postgres\n(`scarab-db-postgres/tests/restart.rs::a_rerun_whose_root_churns_but_whose_content_does_not_still_skips`)\n— but **not on a live cluster**, which is the tier that found the bug.\n\nTwo things to run, both env-gated so neither is in CI:\n\n1. `SCARAB_TEST_KUBE=1` on\n   `crates/scarab-executor-k8s/tests/cluster.rs::workspace_flows_from_a_to_b_through_the_cas`.\n   The assertion the ticket narrowed is restored and widened: it now asserts BOTH\n   that two attempts' snapshot **roots differ** (s7's mtime fidelity) and that\n   their **content identities match** (ADR-0027's determinism). Nobody has seen\n   it pass against a real apiserver.\n\n2. A dogfood rerun that should now **skip** something. Rerun a mid-pipeline step\n   in `.scarab/dogfood.yaml` whose output is byte-identical and confirm a\n   `StepSkipped` event downstream. Before s8 this was structurally impossible —\n   the input signature always changed — so a run where nothing downstream re-runs\n   is the first observation of ADR-0027's headline behaviour actually happening.\n\nWhat would falsify the fix, and is worth looking for specifically:\n\n- the two identities differing on a live Pod. The `scarab.io/workspace-identity`\n  annotation is written by `drive_workspace` in the same patch as the root; an\n  **adopted** Pod (control plane restarted mid-step) takes the\n  `already`-annotated branch and skips the drain entirely, so if the root was\n  written by a pre-s8 binary the identity is absent and the step falls back to\n  root comparison. That is safe (cascade) but it is a real skew path and it\n  should be *seen* rather than assumed.\n- an `outputs:`-declaring step, which is the one Step-boundary path that walks\n  the pruned tree to get its identity (`scarab_storage::content_identity`). Worth\n  a `ws-timing` glance to confirm the walk is not material next to\n  `cas_ingest_ms`.","files":null}]}